    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks. I'm also curious about the subgrade. We're worried the compaction wasn't uniform across the site. How much does improper subgrade compaction contribute to these longitudinal cracks compared to the bitumen/thermal stuff?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Improper subgrade compaction is a significant contributor to longitudinal cracking, often ranking second only to thermal expansion-related issues. Compact subgrades with significant settlement or uneven density can lead to uneven pavement settlement and stress patterns, which exacerbate longitudinal cracking. In many cases, it can be difficult to quantify the exact contribution of subgrade issues versus thermal factors, but poor compaction can be a common underlying cause.",
